						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#224">Shadows of Honor Charter</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Shadows Of Honor Charter 5 parts <br />
<br />
                           Where the value of every outlook....will not bring harm or<br />
                           censure back upon the guild. <br />
<br />
                           Each of us who are enjoying Ever Quest and looking for<br />
                           &quot;the right fit&quot; in a guild has personal reasons for doing<br />
                           so, along with the practical reasons which are stated in<br />
                           the charter below. Those reasons vary from person to<br />
                           person, but we felt it may be helpful for others to know<br />
                           our visions, to understand the foundation of this guild,<br />
                           and perhaps to share with us part of what drives us to<br />
                           build it. Most of us, and certainly our officers, have been<br />
                           in other guilds in the past, guilds that have disappointed<br />
                           us. We are striving to make sure that those disappointing<br />
                           elements are not present in our new guild, Shadows of<br />
                           Honor. We will draw upon the experience of our high level<br />
                           alts for leadership to that end. <br />
<br />
                           Charter: <br />
                           Shadows of Honor was founded on the ideals of family<br />
                           and equality. Shadows of Honor are a group of<br />
                           adventurers bound together by the common calling to<br />
                           fight evil and to spread good, anonymously, as good<br />
                           deeds are meant to be done in order to give grace to the<br />
                           receiver, throughout Norrath. Above all else, Shadows of<br />
                           Honor values honor, fairness, compassion and<br />
                           harmonious fellowship. To be a member of Shadows of<br />
                           Honor is akin to being in a loving family, held together by<br />
                           the unbreakable bonds of friendship and loyalty. <br />
<br />
                           It will be fun and intersting, not to mention rewarding, to<br />
                           develop ways of helping others anonymously. Examples:<br />
                           Healing or buffing someone from afar, or in a crowd;<br />
                           killing a mob then running away quickly; presenting a gift<br />
                           and saying something like &quot;that druid who just passed by<br />
                           here asked me to give you this&quot;, then gate or run away,<br />
                           as if in a hurry. <br />
<br />
                           Try to put SOME roleplay into this, develop your own EQ <br />
                           Shadows &quot;personality&quot;, (as part of the vision). <br />
<br />
<br />
<br />
                                            Guild History <br />
                           Unseen, Sindee Oxxwind whispers, <br />
                           &quot;&quot;We shall be a mighty force against evil. As Shadows,<br />
                           we are barely noticed gliding through Norrath spreading<br />
                           cheer, goodwill, fortune and aid to all, in fairness and<br />
                           humility, bringing honor to our family.&quot;
						</td>
					</tr>
