			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#223">Guild merger</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							There have been many discussions about needing  more members in OOD. We are truly selective in our efforts to only invite only the best that Norrath has to offer. In keeping these ideals in mind I want to anounce that the Shadows of Honor have asked us to invite them as a guild into our ranks. Sindee the Guild Leader has a fine group of players and is looking forward to the future of SoH. She feels that the Shadows can best be served by joining with us. There has been  much discussion between the OOD officers and myself and we agree they bring people of high calibur, and we can provide the expierence from being the oldest guild on Rodcet Nife. I now post their charter so everyone may see where the Shadows of  Honor come from. I welcome them with open arms and look forward to the joining of our guilds. Sindee the guild leader of Soh will be a co-guild leader with the full rights and responsibilities that go with the honor. The   transition of SoH into OOD should be as painless as possible. In the meantime seek out the Shadows and group with them, they will do the same as well. This will give OOD the chance to become an uber guild able<br />
 to take a plain for  themselves, this does not mean that alliences will be forgotton both guilds have many friends and these will  continue. Join me in welcoming the Shadows  into our circle of honor, freindship and loyalty. The sum of the parts will be more than each individual part. Their strengths will become ours. and they will becoome part of us, <br />
                          Nokyli Soulstalker. Guild Leader Order of the Dragon.
						</td>
					</tr>
